{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_015RekW4CXp8yLkozb99ZVT1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the commit `c9b1a99` is the most recent commit that includes changes to `site/src/app/globals.css` with 29 additions. This is the commit that was the previous attempt for US-178 (iter 140). \n\nBut the story still has `passes: false`. This means the changes to globals.css were committed, but the `passes` field in prd.json was never updated to `true`.\n\nLooking at the diff stats for that commit: `prd.json | 2 +-` - it only changed 2 lines in prd.json, but the diff guard probably caught the huge number of .spiral/ file changes.\n\n\nThe real problem is that the previous ralph agent staged all the files together, including the .spiral/ directory, which ballooned the diff to 17,126 lines and exceeded the 500-line limit. The globals.css changes themselves were fine, but they got bundled with all those extra files.\n\nNow I need to figure out what's actually in the current prd.json - whether it already reflects the US-178 completion from iteration 140 or if I need to update it myself. The git status shows prd.json has unstaged modifications, so I should check what the working tree version contains for US-178.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1352,"cache_read_input_tokens":36757,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1352},"output_tokens":15,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c20c525-f94e-437f-8820-d67d1831d206","uuid":"876605f1-add1-4104-bba3-dcf75bbef7fe"}
